course: dictionary
lesson: 10422
title: Triumph: the win and the joy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Triumph is a word full of happy feelings. In «Truth alone triumphs», the words around it tell you what it means: truth wins in the end. Swap your meaning into the sentence: «Truth alone wins» still makes sense, so triumph means to win or succeed.
explain: Triumph can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a triumph is a great success: «The concert was a triumph.» As a verb, to triumph is to win or beat something hard: «Good triumphs over evil.» Look at the words around it to tell which one it is.
explain: Triumph can also mean the joy and pride you feel after you win, like a shout of triumph. Clues such as shout, cheered or proud tell you that a feeling is meant, not just a result.
explain: You can have a triumph of any size, from a hero in a story to a team that works together. If everyone helped and the team won, that win is a triumph of teamwork.
fact: Triumph can be a noun (a triumph) or a verb (to triumph).
fact: «Triumph» means a great victory or success, or the great joy you feel when you win.
fact: «Triumph over» means to beat something difficult.
fact: In ancient Rome, a triumph was a grand parade through the city to honour a winning general.
fact: «Satyameva jayate» is India's national motto, and it means «Truth alone triumphs».
exercise: In the motto «Truth alone triumphs», what does triumphs mean? | Makes a loud noise | *Wins or succeeds in the end | Hides away and gets lost | Gets smaller and smaller
exercise: Mia says, «The concert was a triumph!» What does triumph mean here? | A dreadful mistake | *A great success | A long, boring wait | A small cough
exercise: «Good triumphs over evil in the story.» What does triumphs over mean? | *Beats | Joins with | Runs away from | Hides from
test: «The team cheered in triumph when the goal went in.» What does in triumph suggest? | In a long, boring line | Quietly and slowly | With a lost, sad face | *With great joy and pride after winning
test: In ancient Rome, what was a triumph? | A school exam | A quiet walk in the countryside | *A grand parade through the city to honour a winning general | A type of small boat
exam: Which sentence uses triumph as a verb? | The concert was a triumph. | The triumph was loud and bright. | *The hero will triumph over the dragon in the end. | She felt a shout of triumph.
